{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "crl": "CRL-20261103-003",
  "repository": "root",
  "title": "MZ-065 and MZ-098 integrated Root release",
  "request": "Release the reviewed Root fixes for authoritative temporary check-in linkage and complete ordinary fixed-expense monthly snapshot selection together, without uploading the historical ledger or performing production data repair.",
  "outcome": "Completed same-day checkouts remain valid explicit link targets for temporary check-ins under one server-authoritative fail-closed contract, while ordinary and zero-value consumables again enter the existing idempotent current-month snapshot flow alongside unchanged Referral behavior.",
  "implementation": [
    "Add one authenticated SELECT-only checkout-candidate contract and reuse its order, lifecycle, occupancy, and ambiguity predicate in the locked manual check-in create transaction.",
    "Keep completed, inspected, cleaned, and keys-hung checkout sources linkable without reopening them, while rejecting invalid, occupied, wrong-boundary, or ambiguous sources.",
    "Move the Web manual check-in flow to the Root candidate contract with loading and error fail-closed behavior, stale-response isolation, conflict refresh, and form-input retention.",
    "Restore one shared recurring-template predicate for ordinary fixed expenses, fixed income, zero-value templates, and unpaid Referral percentage refresh candidates.",
    "Keep the existing authorized recurring page's current-month write-on-load flow and idempotent ensure-snapshot endpoint; add no scheduler, schema change, or write-on-read behavior to the revenue or property-expense pages."
  ],
  "impact_dependencies": [
    "The MZ-065 Mobile behavior depends on the paired mobile/CRL-20261103-005 candidate and Root must merge first.",
    "MZ-098 has no cross-repository runtime dependency and changes no API, schema, migration, permission, environment, package, or native input.",
    "October and November missing production snapshots remain untouched and require a separate exact dry-run and production-write authorization."
  ],
  "validation": [
    "MZ-065 backend loopback contract and Web candidate selection passed; a dedicated loopback PostgreSQL 16 database plus two concurrent real HTTP requests proved exactly one active linked check-in and one task-created event, with the loser returning 409 and no deadlock.",
    "MZ-098 recurring-payment rules passed 9 tests; byte-identical source evidence on the same base proved three concurrent real Express requests create one AUD 60 snapshot and a zero-value template creates one zero snapshot in isolated PostgreSQL 16.",
        "CI=true npm run check:full passed the complete Root chain, Web 57 files / 314 tests, and the exact paired Mobile candidate 84 suites / 826 tests; exact ledger/registry/diff gates passed."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Physical-device linkage, real browser account flow, and weak-network behavior remain unverified; isolated PostgreSQL concurrency uses synthetic local-only data.",
    "Snapshot generation remains current-month and page-triggered; historical or unopened-month gaps are not repaired by this release.",
    "No production API, finance page with write side effects, database repair, deployment, or OTA action is part of this candidate.",
    "The historical ledger remains byte-for-byte unchanged and is not included in this change."
  ],
